WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:11.676
When Ben woke up the next morning, he felt better.

2
00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:17.065
Uncle Bert peered at him. "Are you sure you feel okay?"

3
00:00:17.066 --> 00:00:20.884
"Yes," Ben said. "Besides, I can't miss another rehearsal.

4
00:00:20.885 --> 00:00:23.839
Opening night is next weekend."

5
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.447
"I understand," Uncle Bert said.

6
00:00:26.448 --> 00:00:29.528
"But I want you to take some power punch with you.

7
00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:32.665
Drink it if you start to feel tired again."

8
00:00:32.666 --> 00:00:38.291
"I will," Ben promised. Uncle Bert tucked a bottle into Ben's backpack.

9
00:00:38.292 --> 00:00:46.016
Ben gulped down a lizard tongue omelet and headed to school.

10
00:00:46.017 --> 00:00:49.388
*** By the end of the school day, Ben was

11
00:00:49.389 --> 00:00:52.424
exhausted. "I'll drink some power punch," he

12
00:00:52.425 --> 00:00:56.444
thought. "I don't need more problems at rehearsal

13
00:00:56.445 --> 00:01:00.723
today." Ben had just finished the drink when Waldo

14
00:01:00.724 --> 00:01:04.403
approached. "I'm so glad you're drinking my potion," Waldo

15
00:01:04.404 --> 00:01:09.166
said. "Actually, this is my uncle's . . ." Ben's words trailed off as he looked at the bottle.

16
00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:15.951
"Oh no!" Ben slammed his locker shut and slumped to the floor.

17
00:01:15.952 --> 00:01:23.106
He'd forgotten to dump Waldo's potion—Uncle Bert must have mixed them up!

18
00:01:23.107 --> 00:01:28.619
"Don't worry," Waldo said. "It's going to work this time."

19
00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:33.696
"It better work, or else . . ." Suddenly Ben thought of something.

20
00:01:33.697 --> 00:01:39.823
"Hey, remember that time we walked to the park and it was raining out?"

21
00:01:39.824 --> 00:01:44.465
"Um, not really," Waldo replied.

22
00:01:44.466 --> 00:01:50.894
"We passed three blue cars and seven gray ones," Ben said.

23
00:01:50.895 --> 00:01:56.058
"Oh, and there was a dog with a pink collar at the corner. Remember?"

24
00:01:56.059 --> 00:01:58.777
"I don't." Waldo smiled.

25
00:01:58.778 --> 00:02:02.576
"But you do, and that's all that matters.

26
00:02:02.577 --> 00:02:05.345
Come on, let's get to rehearsal!"

27
00:02:05.346 --> 00:02:09.913
*** In the auditorium Ben asked Waldo to run lines with

28
00:02:09.914 --> 00:02:15.059
him. To his astonishment, he had finally memorized

29
00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.597
them! "See?" Waldo said

30
00:02:17.598 --> 00:02:20.560
proudly. "I told you the memory potion would

31
00:02:20.561 --> 00:02:24.517
work. Your scene with Gaby is next. You'll do

32
00:02:24.518 --> 00:02:29.645
great!" Ben floated onstage, feeling confident for the first time in

33
00:02:29.646 --> 00:02:33.997
weeks. "Glad you're back, Ben," Victoria said, but she looked

34
00:02:33.998 --> 00:02:37.396
worried. "Are you sure you're all

35
00:02:37.397 --> 00:02:39.902
right?" "Never better!" Ben

36
00:02:39.903 --> 00:02:43.569
said. "Then let's begin.

37
00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:48.181
Curtain!" Ben bowed to Gaby. "'My dear,'" he

38
00:02:48.182 --> 00:02:49.990
began. "'Duncan comes here

39
00:02:49.991 --> 00:02:53.861
tonight. And when does he leave? Tomorrow. Oh! Never shall

40
00:02:53.862 --> 00:03:01.133
I—'" "Stop!" Victoria shouted. "'And when does he leave?' is Gaby's

41
00:03:01.134 --> 00:03:04.501
line." "Oops." Ben blushed.

42
00:03:04.502 --> 00:03:06.866
"Sorry." "Start again,

43
00:03:06.867 --> 00:03:09.845
please." Ben cleared his

44
00:03:09.846 --> 00:03:15.444
throat. "'My dear. Duncan comes here tonight. And when does he leave?

45
00:03:15.445 --> 00:03:19.097
Oh—'" "Ben!" Gaby said. "You did it

46
00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:23.226
again!" Ben hit the side of his head. His memory was in overdrive.

47
00:03:23.227 --> 00:03:26.243
"I'll get it right this time," he promised.

48
00:03:26.244 --> 00:03:30.745
But he didn't get it right that time or the next four times either.

49
00:03:30.746 --> 00:03:40.206
The witches were standing in the wings laughing hysterically as he messed up over and over again.

50
00:03:40.207 --> 00:03:44.298
And Victoria and Gaby were starting to run out of patience.

51
00:03:44.299 --> 00:03:53.478
"Let me try it one more time," Ben pleaded. "I know I can do it."

52
00:03:53.479 --> 00:03:59.046
But he didn't do it, and this time, Gaby got so angry, she stomped her foot.

53
00:03:59.047 --> 00:04:02.677
Smash! She'd put a huge hole in the stage.

54
00:04:02.678 --> 00:04:05.870
"That's it!" Victoria cried.

55
00:04:05.871 --> 00:04:09.714
"I've never seen a cast with such terrible luck!"

56
00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:13.602
Ozzy grinned. "It's the curse!"

57
00:04:13.603 --> 00:04:17.454
Ben hung his head. "Maybe I'm the curse."

58
00:04:17.455 --> 00:04:24.550
"That's not true," Jen said as Victoria beckoned to her.

59
00:04:24.551 --> 00:04:28.477
"Jen, please go get Mr. Freaky," Victoria said.

60
00:04:28.478 --> 00:04:32.354
"I can't work like this for one more second!"

61
00:04:32.355 --> 00:04:37.217
Jen walked away while everyone else stood frozen in place.

62
00:04:37.218 --> 00:04:41.506
Even the three witches were silent, no longer mocking Ben.

63
00:04:41.507 --> 00:04:43.361
Victoria clapped.

64
00:04:43.362 --> 00:04:48.813
"I want everyone onstage, right now! Just watch out for that hole."

65
00:04:48.814 --> 00:04:51.611
The entire cast and crew scurried onstage.

66
00:04:51.612 --> 00:04:54.470
Ben tried to hide behind everyone else.

67
00:04:54.471 --> 00:04:59.319
"If I had learned my lines the right way," he thought, "none of this would have happened."

68
00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:03.094
But another part of him was wondering about the curse of Macdeath

69
00:05:03.095 --> 00:05:05.533
. Could that be to blame

70
00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:11.442
too? "My darling monsters," Victoria began, "you have so much

71
00:05:11.443 --> 00:05:15.337
promise. But we have very little time before opening

72
00:05:15.338 --> 00:05:21.359
night. And I, Victoria Lafang, have a reputation to uphold. If you

73
00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:29.298
can't—" "What in the world is going on?" Mr. Freaky dashed into the auditorium, his noses wiggling.

74
00:05:29.299 --> 00:05:33.814
"It sounds like this play is completely out of control!"

75
00:05:33.815 --> 00:05:36.888
He frowned at the cast and crew members.

76
00:05:36.889 --> 00:05:41.490
"I warned you students about behaving for Ms. Lafang!"

77
00:05:41.491 --> 00:05:43.792
Then he turned to Victoria.

78
00:05:43.793 --> 00:05:50.601
"I am so sorry! Normally everything at Monster Academy is totally under control."

79
00:05:50.602 --> 00:05:55.124
He took out his handkerchief and blew his noses.

80
00:05:55.125 --> 00:05:57.555
Victoria patted him on the shoulder.

81
00:05:57.556 --> 00:06:01.712
"It's okay, Mr. Freaky. You don't need to get upset."

82
00:06:01.713 --> 00:06:04.414
Winnie cleared her throat.

83
00:06:04.415 --> 00:06:07.424
"Some things are going well, Mr. Freaky.

84
00:06:07.425 --> 00:06:10.602
The costumes and scenery are ready.

85
00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:14.150
We just have to finish making the witches' cauldron."

86
00:06:14.151 --> 00:06:19.176
"Thank goodness for that!" Mr. Freaky put away his handkerchief.

87
00:06:19.177 --> 00:06:28.808
"Now the rest of you had better shape up, or this will be the last play Monster Academy ever performs!"

